          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#categorical_semantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of existential quantification is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (-1)-truncation
            of the
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            morphism that projects out the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+variable"} free variable
            over which the existental quantifier quantifies.
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q[\hat{x}]
            corresponds to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(T) \times A \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(T)
            is the interpretation of the type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the interpretation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            read in context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
