          %p
            (Often we have a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/display+maps"} display maps
            and require
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to be one of these.) Alternatively, any pullback functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast\colon Set/A \to Set/B
            can be construed as pulling back along an object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = (f \colon B \to A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !\colon X \to 1
            corresponding to an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the slice
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/B \simeq (Set/A)/X
          %p
            Therefore in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of a suitable category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            (with sufficient pullbacks)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is given by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
                object of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over-topos"} over-topos
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
                object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                itself.
          %p
            Existential quantification is essentially the restriction of the extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            of a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+geometric+morphism"} étale geometric morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\ast
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo !
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (X_!\dashv X^*\dashv X_*):\mathcal{E}/X
                  \\stackrel{\overset{X_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{X^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{X_*}{\to}}}
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
            is the functor that takes an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            projection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon X \times A \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo !
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_! = \Sigma_X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            (i.e., forgetful functor taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to X
            to
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\ast = \Pi_X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            operation that is right adjoint to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
          %p
            The dependent sum operation restricts to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            by pre- and postcomposition with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ≤
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_{\leq -1} \mathcal{E}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\tau_{\leq -1}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{}{\hookrightarrow}}
                  \\mathcal{E}
          %p
            to give existential quantification over the domain (or context)
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo *
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo *
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo !
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℰ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi τ
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mo ≤
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                        %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi τ
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mo ≤
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                        %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ≤
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mo ∀
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ∃
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ≤
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                          %mi ℰ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{E}/X
                  \&amp;
                  \\stackrel{\overset{X_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{X^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{X_*}{\to}}}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\\
                  {}^\mathllap{\tau_{\leq_{-1}}}\downarrow \uparrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  {}^\mathllap{\tau_{\leq_{-1}}}\downarrow \uparrow
                  \\\
                  \\tau_{\leq_{-1}}
                  \\mathcal{E}/X
                  \&amp;
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\exists}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\forall}{\to}}}
                  \&amp;
                  \\tau_{\leq_{-1}} \mathcal{E}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In other words, we obtain the existential quantifier by applying the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncating
            the result. This is equivalent to constructing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
          %p
            Dually, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image+functor"} direct image functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall
            (dependent product) expresses the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
            = succeed "-truncated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
          %p
            The same makes verbatim sense also in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-logic"} (∞,1)-logic
            of any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            This interpretation of existential quantification as the left adjoint to context extension is also used in the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
          %h3#frobenius_reciprocity Frobenius reciprocity
          %p
            The existential quantifier and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            are related via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            does not have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+variable"} free variable
            then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi x
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ψ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exists_x (\phi \wedge \psi)
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  (\exists_x \phi) \wedge \psi
                  \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{N}
            be the set of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \coloneqq 2\mathbb{N} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{N}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of even natural numbers. This expresses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi IsEven
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x) \coloneqq IsEven(x)
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\phi \in Set/{\mathbb{N}})
                  \\mapsto
                  (\sum_{x\colon X} \phi(x) \in Set)
          %p
            is simply the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \mathbb{N} \in Set
            of even natural numbers. Since this is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} (-1)-truncation
            is therefore the singleton set, hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
          %p
            Notice that before the
            = succeed "-truncation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
            %em that
            there is an even number, but it remembers “all proofs that there is one”, namely every example of an even number.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/possibility"}> possibility
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/example"} example
            %li
              %p
