          %h2#references References
          %p
            The observation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            forms an
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            with the existantial/universal quantifiers is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adjointness+in+Foundations"} Adjointness in Foundations
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/reprints/articles/16/tr16abs.html"} TAC
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantifiers and sheaves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mathunion.org/fileadmin/ICM/Proceedings/ICM1970.1/ICM1970.1.ocr.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and further developed to the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrines"} hyperdoctrines
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equality in hyperdoctrines and comprehension schema as an adjoint functor
          %p The definition of the existential quantifier in dependent type theory as the propositional truncation of the dependent sum type is found in:
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , §3.7 in:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
          %p And the existential quantifier defined from the type of propositions and dependent product types can be found in:
          %ul
            %li
              Madeleine Birchfield,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Constructing coproduct types and boolean types from universes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/457904/constructing-coproduct-types-and-boolean-types-from-universes"} web
        .revisedby
